.TH PROFILE.D 4 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
profile.d \- the packages' additions to the login environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BI /etc/profile.d/ package .sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
At the end of
.BR /etc/profile ,
a login shell reads every readable file in
.B /etc/profile.d
whose name ends in
.BR .sh ,
in name order.
A package that needs something in every user's environment, such as a
directory on
.BR PATH ,
ships one such file instead of editing
.BR /etc/profile .
Each file is read by the user's login shell
.RB ( sh
or
.BR ksh ),
so it must be plain Bourne shell, and it should change nothing when it is
read twice.
A file with another name, such as
.BR name.sh.off ,
is not read.
.PP
The base package ships
.BR amix-base.sh ,
which puts
.B /usr/amix/bin
on
.B PATH
just before
.BR /usr/bin .
That directory holds only commands that answer for the add-on packages'
files and pass everything else to the stock command of the same name, such
as
.BR man (1).
.B /usr/local/bin
stays first, and the add-on packages' own
.B /opt/amix/bin
stays last, so stock commands keep their place.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/profile.d/amix-base.sh
the base package's addition.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR profile (4),
.BR man (1)
